                                                "sense_id": "6d9ee33c-f30c-3b99-b411-3eefe68acc2f",
                                                "text": "Soloman's belief that love is necessarily paradoxical issues from his attempt to define it as what Sartre would call a dialectical metastability. Love must therefore be not a \"state of the union but a never ending conflict of pushing away and pulling together.\""
                                            }
